WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.226
Squeeze an agent's weights to four bits, and it loses about seven

00:00:04.226 --> 00:00:05.778
points across five agent benchmarks.

00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:07.330
Where do those points go?

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.373
Hi, I'm Wilder!

00:00:11.373 --> 00:00:15.359
Today, a training method that keeps a four-bit agent close to its

00:00:15.359 --> 00:00:18.349
full-precision self, by making it fix its own mistakes.

00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:20.795
Chapter one.

00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:21.952
Where the points go.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.493
Start with a toy.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:30.499
Say each turn of a task goes right with probability p.

00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:33.968
If the task needs k turns and any wrong one sinks it,

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.255
the task succeeds with p to the power k.

00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:38.410
A single-turn benchmark measures p.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.226
An agent benchmark measures p to the k, so small losses

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:43.614
per turn get multiplied.

00:00:45.942 --> 00:00:50.700
At ninety-nine percent per turn, twenty turns still succeed eighty-two percent of the time.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.090
Drop to ninety-seven percent per turn.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:57.687
That is two points on a single question, and twenty-seven points at twenty turns.

00:00:58.107 --> 00:01:00.400
This is my arithmetic, not the paper's.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.348
Real turns are not independent, but the shape holds.

00:01:05.217 --> 00:01:08.444
The paper calls the first wrong turn a behavioral divergence.

00:01:08.444 --> 00:01:12.962
Asked to book a train with no route, the full-precision model asks where to.

00:01:13.382 --> 00:01:17.945
On-Policy QAD invents a route from Boston to New York, and asks for tickets.

00:01:18.365 --> 00:01:23.817
Plain GPTQ invents San Francisco to Los Angeles, then asks the user to confirm.

00:01:25.425 --> 00:01:26.261
Chapter two.

00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:27.515
Steer, verify, keep.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.542
Here's the idea.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:35.165
The full-precision teacher hints at the failing turn.

00:01:35.165 --> 00:01:38.772
The student writes its own fix, which is kept only if

00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:40.083
running it checks out.

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:41.723
Then training removes the hint.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.519
Here is a task as a row of turns.

00:01:46.519 --> 00:01:48.565
On top, the teacher's successful run.

00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:53.339
Below, the four-bit student, which parts ways where its action changes the environment differently.

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:55.496
Restore everything before that turn.

00:01:55.496 --> 00:01:58.971
The teacher writes a steering prompt, and the student retries.

00:01:58.971 --> 00:02:02.793
This attempt fails the check, so the teacher refines the prompt.

00:02:03.213 --> 00:02:07.208
The next attempt moves the environment exactly as the reference did.

00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:10.476
It passes local verification, and the fix is kept.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.220
Then the student carries on with no prompt.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.125
If it slips again, the loop finds the next divergence.

00:02:16.545 --> 00:02:17.605
Training uses both.

00:02:17.605 --> 00:02:21.846
At the corrected turn, the target is the student with the prompt.

00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:23.613
Everywhere else, the full-precision teacher.

00:02:25.675 --> 00:02:28.901
In this training case, the student calls cat on a file

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.074
from its home folder.

00:02:30.074 --> 00:02:33.006
The tool reads only the current directory, so it fails.

00:02:33.426 --> 00:02:37.763
The teacher's prompt gives a rule: navigate to the workspace directory before reading.

00:02:37.763 --> 00:02:39.764
It never writes the call itself.

00:02:40.184 --> 00:02:43.797
From the restored state, the student checks where it is, changes directory,

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:45.001
and reads the file.

00:02:45.421 --> 00:02:48.049
The check compares the result with the reference.

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:51.663
The directory moved the same way and the file text matches.

00:02:51.663 --> 00:02:51.991
Accepted.

00:02:53.925 --> 00:02:58.468
In the released code, the database is saved before and after every turn.

00:02:58.468 --> 00:03:00.564
Both copies must match the reference's.

00:03:00.984 --> 00:03:04.127
If the reference's turn changed the state, matching it is enough.

00:03:04.547 --> 00:03:07.198
If it only read, the returned result must match too.

00:03:08.675 --> 00:03:09.309
Chapter three.

00:03:09.309 --> 00:03:10.577
Training the hint away.

00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:17.669
The learner, q, sees the history with every prompt removed.

00:03:18.089 --> 00:03:21.349
At a corrected turn it matches the frozen student that did see

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:22.708
the prompt, with forward KL.

00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:25.696
So it learns to act as if the hint were there.

00:03:26.116 --> 00:03:30.166
Everywhere else it stays close to the full-precision teacher, with reverse KL.

00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:33.879
Swapping the two directions costs about two and a half points.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.349
Chapter four.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.448
Does it hold up?

00:03:41.883 --> 00:03:47.355
On Qwen three, eight billion, full precision averages fifty-three point five four.

00:03:47.355 --> 00:03:49.635
GPTQ, forty-six point three six.

00:03:49.635 --> 00:03:51.460
The best baseline, fifty-one.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.740
SteerDistill, fifty-three point one eight.

00:03:55.425 --> 00:03:59.691
The authors' own animation of the loop: guidance, retry, verification, and a

00:03:59.691 --> 00:04:01.824
refine arrow when the check fails.

00:04:02.244 --> 00:04:03.403
Then the cost.

00:04:03.403 --> 00:04:08.424
Thirty-two GPU hours reach thirty-one point six eight percent on tau squared bench.

00:04:08.424 --> 00:04:13.058
The strongest baseline needs ninety-six hours to reach twenty-nine point eight four.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.784
The one-point claim is true as stated.

00:04:16.784 --> 00:04:18.130
Here is where it bends.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.116
It holds for the average.

00:04:20.116 --> 00:04:23.875
On Gemma, two benchmarks sit just over a point under full precision.

00:04:24.295 --> 00:04:25.969
It holds at four-bit weights.

00:04:25.969 --> 00:04:29.652
With eight-bit activations the gap nears two points, and at two-bit

00:04:29.652 --> 00:04:30.991
weights it passes ten.

00:04:31.411 --> 00:04:34.748
And it needs a teacher that solves the task, and an environment

00:04:34.748 --> 00:04:36.139
you can snapshot and restore.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.889
Spend the recovery on the turn where the state first diverges, and

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:43.249
make the compressed model write its own fix.

00:04:46.025 --> 00:04:46.683
To recap.

00:04:46.683 --> 00:04:48.986
One wrong turn sinks a long task.

00:04:48.986 --> 00:04:51.618
Hint, verify by running it, keep the fix.

00:04:51.618 --> 00:04:55.895
At four-bit weights, it lands within a point of full precision, on average.

00:04:56.315 --> 00:04:58.398
Every source is in the full article.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:58.993
I'm Wilder.

00:04:58.993 --> 00:04:59.291
Bye!
